From 30152033016aa9aa81f8675716857daee04cd0d5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jolyon Brown <jolyon@limilo.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 01:42:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Far spaces: warning 2026 for a far pointer passed through ...

A variadic argument has no parameter type, so a far array or a pointer
into a far space went to the callee as it was, and va_arg read it as a
near pointer, with no warning: nethack64's get_compopt_value(),
Sprintf(buf, "%s", to_be_done), a function's static string moved to
far space 5 by #pragma fardefault. Such an argument is now reported as
a conversion out of its space, as an assignment to a near pointer is
(the character space excepted, as there). make check 1,706 of 1,706,
no new failures.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 oscar64/InterCodeGenerator.cpp | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/oscar64/InterCodeGenerator.cpp b/oscar64/InterCodeGenerator.cpp
index ccf1a64..81ac9e8 100644
--- a/oscar64/InterCodeGenerator.cpp
+++ b/oscar64/InterCodeGenerator.cpp
@@ -4536,6 +4536,12 @@ InterCodeGenerator::ExValue InterCodeGenerator::TranslateExpression(Declaration*
 						{
 							vr = CoerceType(proc, texp, block, inlineMapper, vr, TheSignedIntTypeDeclaration);
 						}
+						else if (vr.mType->mType == DT_TYPE_ARRAY || vr.mType->mType == DT_TYPE_POINTER)
+						{
+							// a variadic argument goes on as a near pointer (va_arg), with no type to
+							// convert to: printf("%s", far_array) read the far address as near RAM
+							CheckFarConversion(texp, (vr.mType->mType == DT_TYPE_ARRAY || vr.mFarSpace) ? vr.mFarSpace : vr.mType->mBase->FarSpace(), 0);
+						}
 
 
 						InterInstruction* wins = new InterInstruction(MapLocation(exp, inlineMapper), IC_STORE);
-- 
